From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an extension's popup window is the shell's to draw

Three lists, so that the event a `<webview>` dispatches when an extension
asks for a popup window -- `chrome.windows.create({type: "popup", url})`,
which is Bitwarden's sign-in -- is compiled and reaches the page:
`core/html/build.gni` builds `DomicilePopupWindowEvent`, `idl_in_core.gni`
generates its bindings, and `generated_in_core.gni` names the generated pair.

Everything else is new files under src/: the event, the element's
`popupwindow` attribute carried in CreateGuest, the `PopupWindowRequested`
member on WebViewGuestClient, and the desk's popup windows and its
windows.create and windows.remove.

The position in each list is beside patch 0053's file chooser event, and the
context is the lists as 0053 leaves them. The post-image blob hashes are
zeroed, for the reason patch 0035 gives.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium;
`guard-extension-popup-window.sh` measures it on `crux` with the rest of
the engine job.
---
 third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/generated_in_core.gni | 2 ++
 third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/idl_in_core.gni       | 1 +
 third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/build.gni            | 2 ++
 3 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

